  "name": "assemblies",
  "description": "A multi-implementation framework for simulating the Assembly Calculus, a mathematical model of brain computation based on randomly connected neurons and Hebbian plasticity. The project provides efficient C++ and Python kernels for modeling high-level cognitive operations, including association, pattern completion, and hierarchical language parsing. It facilitates research into the computational properties of neuronal assemblies, such as their capacity for Turing-universal computation and language acquisition.",
